{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3448","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3448","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3448\",\"parent_revision\":\"7dcc8211fa1dd6e8263d72a55ad9957be21fd293f67e36198059a93e7e1ecba8\",\"root_revision\":\"7dcc8211fa1dd6e8263d72a55ad9957be21fd293f67e36198059a93e7e1ecba8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThree parts of the dispatch and kage-bunshin path do not work. Each was found by reading the two sides of a contract and observing that they disagree.\\n\\n## 1. The command dispatch builds is rejected by the script it calls\\n\\n`_build_spawn_cmd` (`plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py:1752`) produces:\\n\\n    uv run <spawn.py> --model <model> --name dispatch-<milestone>-<issue> [--effort <e>] [--worktree] [--branch <b>] \\\"<prompt>\\\"\\n\\n`spawn.py` requires a subcommand (`plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py:1174`):\\n\\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\\\"command\\\", metavar=\\\"COMMAND\\\", required=True)\\n\\nThe built command carries no subcommand token, so argparse reads `--model`'s value as the COMMAND choice. Neither `--worktree` nor `--branch` is defined anywhere in that parser.\\n\\n## 2. The PID column that liveness checking reads is never written\\n\\n`DispatchStateManager.check_stale_pids` (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py:402-458`) selects `WHERE status = 'in-progress' AND pid IS NOT NULL` and calls `os.kill(pid, 0)` on each row.\\n\\n`_build_spawn_record` (`spawn.py:677-686`) is the sole producer of the JSON the dispatch caller parses. It emits `name`, `tmux_session`, `model`, `spawned_at`, `worktree`, and optionally `session_id`. It emits no `pid`. The caller defaults the value to `-1` and guards on `if pid > 0`, so the column stays NULL and the query matches no rows.\\n\\n## 3. Three hooks read a state path spawn.py does not write\\n\\nHooks read `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/kage-bunshin/registry-{session_id}.json`:\\n\\n- `hooks/session-end-kage-bunshin-cleanup.cjs:82`\\n- `hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs:130`\\n- `hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs:81`\\n\\nspawn.py writes `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/kage-bunshin/sessions/{session_id}/{name}.json` (`spawn.py:23,200,221`). Its own header comment records that older registry files \\\"left from prior runs are ignored\\\".\\n\\nEach hook read sits inside `try { ... } catch { exit(0) }`, so the miss produces no error.\\n\\n## Further observation in the same path\\n\\n`_dispatch_db_path` (`dh_core/operations.py:1567-1573`) builds its project stub with `str(project_root).lstrip(\\\"/\\\").replace(\\\"/\\\", \\\"-\\\")`. `dh_paths.compute_slug` (`dh_paths.py:375-387`) keeps the leading `-`, and its docstring records that as intentional. The dispatch database therefore lands in a different project directory from every other DH state artifact.\\n\\nThe same dispatch stack exists as two near-verbatim copies, in `dh_core/operations.py` and `backlog_core/server.py`.\\n\\n## Where observed\\n\\nRead on branch `worktree-melodic-plotting-emerson`, 2026-09-06. Neither `dispatch-state.db` nor a `kage-bunshin/` directory exists under `~/.dh/projects/` on the machine used, so no live run was available to observe end to end.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nA dispatched wave item cannot reach a running session. The stale-PID sweep meant to detect a worker that died reports nothing, because it queries a column nothing populates. The SessionEnd hook responsible for cleaning up orphaned tmux sessions finds no sessions and removes none, silently.\\n\\nExisting tests do not surface any of this: the dispatch tests supply a PID directly to `set_item_in_progress` and mock `os.kill`, so they never exercise the spawn.py contract.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: all three trace to one change, `78a4d1269 refactor(kage-bunshin): replace FIFO+stream-json with interactive tmux sessions`, which altered spawn.py's CLI surface, its output record and its storage path together while the consumers stayed on the previous contract. Not confirmed \u2014 that commit has not been diffed against the three consumers.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA dispatched wave item cannot reach a running session. The stale-PID sweep meant to detect a worker that died reports nothing, because it queries a column nothing populates. The SessionEnd hook responsible for cleaning up orphaned tmux sessions finds no sessions and removes none, silently.\\n\\nExisting tests do not surface any of this: the dispatch tests supply a PID directly to `set_item_in_progress` and mock `os.kill`, so they never exercise the spawn.py contract.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: all three trace to one change, `78a4d1269 refactor(kage-bunshin): replace FIFO+stream-json with interactive tmux sessions`, which altered spawn.py's CLI surface, its output record and its storage path together while the consumers stayed on the previous contract. Not confirmed \u2014 that commit has not been diffed against the three consumers.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session audit of the dispatch and kage-bunshin path, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## 3 Three Hooks Read A State Path Spawn Py Does Not Write\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nHooks read `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/kage-bunshin/registry-{session_id}.json`:\\n\\n- `hooks/session-end-kage-bunshin-cleanup.cjs:82`\\n- `hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs:130`\\n- `hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs:81`\\n\\nspawn.py writes `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/kage-bunshin/sessions/{session_id}/{name}.json` (`spawn.py:23,200,221`). Its own header comment records that older registry files \\\"left from prior runs are ignored\\\".\\n\\nEach hook read sits inside `try { ... } catch { exit(0) }`, so the miss produces no error.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Further Observation In The Same Path\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`_dispatch_db_path` (`dh_core/operations.py:1567-1573`) builds its project stub with `str(project_root).lstrip(\\\"/\\\").replace(\\\"/\\\", \\\"-\\\")`. `dh_paths.compute_slug` (`dh_paths.py:375-387`) keeps the leading `-`, and its docstring records that as intentional. The dispatch database therefore lands in a different project directory from every other DH state artifact.\\n\\nThe same dispatch stack exists as two near-verbatim copies, in `dh_core/operations.py` and `backlog_core/server.py`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRead on branch `worktree-melodic-plotting-emerson`, 2026-09-06. Neither `dispatch-state.db` nor a `kage-bunshin/` directory exists under `~/.dh/projects/` on the machine used, so no live run was available to observe end to end.\\n</div>\\n\\n## 1 The Command Dispatch Builds Is Rejected By The Script It Calls\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`_build_spawn_cmd` (`plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py:1752`) produces:\\n\\n    uv run <spawn.py> --model <model> --name dispatch-<milestone>-<issue> [--effort <e>] [--worktree] [--branch <b>] \\\"<prompt>\\\"\\n\\n`spawn.py` requires a subcommand (`plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py:1174`):\\n\\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\\\"command\\\", metavar=\\\"COMMAND\\\", required=True)\\n\\nThe built command carries no subcommand token, so argparse reads `--model`'s value as the COMMAND choice. Neither `--worktree` nor `--branch` is defined anywhere in that parser.\\n</div>\\n\\n## 2 The Pid Column That Liveness Checking Reads Is Never Written\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`DispatchStateManager.check_stale_pids` (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py:402-458`) selects `WHERE status = 'in-progress' AND pid IS NOT NULL` and calls `os.kill(pid, 0)` on each row.\\n\\n`_build_spawn_record` (`spawn.py:677-686`) is the sole producer of the JSON the dispatch caller parses. It emits `name`, `tmux_session`, `model`, `spawned_at`, `worktree`, and optionally `session_id`. It emits no `pid`. The caller defaults the value to `-1` and guards on `if pid > 0`, so the column stays NULL and the query matches no rows.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"fb6483ff0dd716105a6cb9158c119f19471e67ada12cd0e0f7729d0c4e5fe8d6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBjjg\"}"}